{"agent":"i2-kilo","data":{"by":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"In `_unchanged_delta`, when `release(counts)` is called for the newly supported case (failed gate with unrechecked confirmed findings, no unreadable findings, and no untriaged findings), `release` uses `counts` which are passed directly from `GD.triage_counts(it, gate) or {}`. However, `counts` returned by `GD.triage_counts` contains triage keys (such as `untriaged`, `refuted`, `confirmed`, etc.), whereas `_settle_mark` expects a counts dictionary containing status categories such as `refuted` and `fixed`, or whichever keys `_settle_mark` counts. Passing `GD.triage_counts` results in an incorrect dictionary structure being passed to `_settle_mark`, causing a `KeyError` or incorrect settling logic when releasing the gate, which can be demonstrated when a failed gate with confirmed findings is released via this branch.","digest":"2ed78e6b2da29977","family":"google","location":"ddflow/api/review/triaging.py:649","malformed":"","reviewer":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/api/review/triaging.py:649"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"`_unchanged_delta` runs for every tree that matches the reviewed head, not only when a later full review already covered a fix. The new branch releases a failed gate as passed whenever `_unrechecked_confirmed` is non-empty, the records are readable, and nothing is untriaged. Given a review that raises finding 1, the user confirms it, and no commit is made, a delta review hits this path and `release()` records the gate passed, so merge proceeds with the confirmed bug still in the tree — the same inputs the old \"stays failed\" path correctly refused. Nothing in the condition checks that the reviewed head post-dates a fix or that a round actually failed to re-raise the finding.","digest":"a955d4d627717b8e","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/api/review/triaging.py:_unchanged_delta","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/api/review/triaging.py:_unchanged_delta"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":5619,"diff_sha":"36c5d5e4940bdbbfece0997e497e12838f0f38da8eaab1644a27f2043b9c6bf8","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-B-tk-delta-round-empty","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":1.5,"family":"google","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":12000,"model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","output_digest":"f9093afd7dc70bfc","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-tk-delta-round-empty.rubber_duck.gemini-3.5-flash-lite.20261111T131246Z-887c0e83.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_head":"7bae873103b1a679fe62da628d0292012f60d8e4","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/review/triaging.py":"100644 0b8abef66d38ff00158b37cff26a99226776f49d","tests/test_complete_failed_review_gate.py":"100644 888c53dfafe7dedfeb47dbe56af1f23a194b6eb0"},"reviewer":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","reviewer_digest":"c7d1b7506be569ee","reviewer_families":["google","xai"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/api/review/triaging.py:649","ddflow/api/review/triaging.py:_unchanged_delta"],"tree_sha":"7bae873103b1+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"2 finding(s)"},"id":"e4ac80e9c648043c2996e49e8","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":174237,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B-tk-delta-round-empty","ts":"2026-11-11T13:13:52.824133Z"}
